meta {
  name: leads export
  type: http
  seq: 46
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/administrator/leads/export/
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  CSV download of every lead. Responds with `text/csv` and
  `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="vidaverde-leads-20260912.csv"`.

  Unfiltered by design -- it is the whole list, for handing to an email platform.
  Use **leads** with `?subscribed=true` if you only want the mailable ones.

  **Check `Subscribed` before importing anywhere.** A `no` means that person
  used the one-click unsubscribe link, and mailing them again is the thing the
  link exists to prevent.

  Streams with `.iterator()`, so a large list does not load into memory.

  ## API example response
  Captured,First name,Email,Source,Subscribed,Converted
  2026-09-05 09:02,Tess,tess@example.com,homepage,yes,
  2026-09-06 14:31,Tom,curious.learner@example.com,blog_post,yes,2026-09-09
}
